// Feature Audit keymap expectations for emacs (ADR 0152, 0160) — parsed from
// the shipped config.el's map! forms by lib/feature-audit/binds-emacs.awk;
// actions are "<states> <command>" (states: an evil state set, or `leader`
// for SPC binds). The probe starts the user's Doom once as a throwaway
// daemon and asks each chord's key-binding in a buffer in that evil state:
// `resolves` passes when it is the command the config binds ({arg}). That
// proves nvim's map won over Doom's defaults and nothing later clobbered it.
{
  "expect": [
    { "action": "*", "effect": "resolves", "arg": "{arg}" }
  ]
}
